  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nIt seems like you end up with a corrupt matrix HQ room: every few days, the room reappears in your room list, but not correctly: the room has no name then. It is listed with the roomname just \"$some_username and 487 others\" or such and the URL is just like `!cURbafjkfsMDVwdRDQ:matrix.org`  .  \r\nYou can then leave the room again, but after a few days it will reappear again and again.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- using **postgresql** use the [nuke-room-from-db.sh](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/scripts-dev/nuke-room-from-db.sh) script from my PR https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/pull/2337 on the \"Matrix HQ\" room\r\n- This seems to really delete the room, and it will first disappear from your room list in Riot\r\n- wait a few days\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: my own homeserver\r\n- **Version**:       0.26.0\r\n- **Install method**: git clone/pip      \r\n- **Platform**:       \r\n  -  Debian squeeze version 9.3\r\n  - Hardware: Intel Core™ i7-6700 Quad-Core (Hetzner EX41S),  running in a XEN vm/container (xen 4.6)\r\n- Version of riot-web: 0.13.5",
